<title>USA: United orders 8 Boeing 767-300 aircraft.</title>
<headline>United orders 8 Boeing 767-300 aircraft.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UAL Corp's United Airlines unit said it has ordered eight Boeing Co 767-300 aircraft as part of the airline's ongoing fleet replacement program.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The aircraft are powered by Pratt &amp; Whitney PW 4000 engines. Pratt &amp; Whitney is a unit of United Technologies Corp.</p>
<p>The aircraft will be delivered over the next three years with four plans arriving in 1998, one in 1999 and three in 2000, bringing United's fleet of 767-300s to 31, the airline said.</p>
<p>United has completed orders for 111 aircraft that will replace 111 aircraft scheduled for retirement from 1996 through 2002.</p>
<p>United shares were up 5/16 at 73-7/8 Thursday. Boeing shares were up 5/16 at 55-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
